iewing its cited original sources.\nThe union of those settled observations' source_ids must cover EVERY source_ids\nentry of the offered obligation. Review coverage is not a claim that every source\nis a premise of a support: genuinely irrelevant or corrective original text may\nhave a separate sourced review. Never add unsupported citations, classify text\nautomatically, or label supporting evidence irrelevant merely to satisfy coverage.\nAn empty slot does not resolve an earlier issue. Do not assert hypothetical\nwhole-corpus exhaustiveness requirements; scoped sufficient evidence may resolve\na missing-evidence issue without having read every memory.\n\nWhen source_span_columns is present, source_spans contains row arrays. Match each\nrow position to source_span_columns to reconstruct every span object before\nreading. References to source_spans[].id or other fields mean those objects.\nThe id column holds source aliases (sN); doc_id holds the original document ID or,\nwhen source_documents is present, its metadata reference (dN), never source_ids.\n\n\nCURRENT PHASE: HISTORY EVIDENCE. Complete only the supplied historical task and\nrequested variable scopes. This is not the final response-selection stage.\nFor retrieval, extract concrete statements supported by the supplied original\nhistory. For an intermediate compose task, summarize those historical facts,\npreferences, constraints and changes using the supplied parent versions and\noriginal quotations. A history summary describes what the sources establish;\nit must not address the user, offer a new recommendation or draft a reply.\nThe original user utterance provides query context. It is not an instruction to\nanswer it at this stage or to retrieve an exact duplicate of what it already says.\nPublic response options are not available here. Do not invent, compare or refer\nto options A/B/C/D. Return exactly the slots object; no final_prediction or\nsemantic_answer fields belong in a history-evidence response.\nKeep each value within its declared type, entity and time scope. Preserve earlier\nand later attitudes, conditions and supporting quotations; a historical dislike\nmust not silently replace a later documented change. Assistant advice alone does\nnot establish an adopted user preference. Do not invent external catalogues,\navailability or past execution of a future suggestion. A partial observation must\ncite its actual clue. Use unresolved only for a specific condition still necessary\nto establish this requested historical value, not hypothetical exhaustive coverage.\nFor one text-summary variable, synthesize compatible query-relevant facts into one\nsufficient source-grounded whole summary; do not report each event as a different\ncomplete value of that variable. Multiple supports must be alternative sufficient\nproofs of the same whole value. Keep partial evidence, negative experiences and\nvalid counters explicit when a complete scoped summary is not established.\nPositive and negative experiences can both support a historical summary. A sourced\ndislike is useful history, not automatically a contradiction observation: that\nstance is reserved for challenging an identified existing fact route. Preserve\nthe difference between past enjoyment, later frustration and their conditions in\nthe value and citations; do not summarize them as an unconditional current interest.\nRe-read any supplied evidence obligations and their original sources explicitly;\ndo not drop a source or contradiction merely because a prior value is available.\nOnly a variable explicitly declaring evidence_semantics=\"personal_history_summary\"\npermits a source-grounded summary_revision. For compatible added history, preserve\nthe old and new facts, negative experiences and time conditions in the new summary;\nexplicitly name the current old summary routes and version as offered by the\nprotocol. Re-read and cite their original sources together with the new evidence.\nThis retires an old summary representation without asserting that its historical\nfacts were false. A genuine factual refutation remains a contradiction with its\nown sources and targets. Never use summary revision to hide or discard a counter,\nchange scope, choose an arbitrary latest value, or revise the terminal response.\nA personal_atomic_fact variable keeps one scoped factual value. Different sources\nmay independently support that same value; separate compatible events are not\nalternative whole values of an atomic fact. This declaration does not permit summary_revision.\n\nThis request is phase=history_evidence. Its ONLY top-level output field is slots. Do not return semantic_answer, final_prediction, audit_verdict, or any other top-level field, even null. Read or summarize the requested scoped historical evidence; do not write a conversational reply or invent candidate responses.\n\nAn explicitly declared personal_history_summary is a revisable representation of\nsourced history. Compatible additional facts do not contradict the older facts.\nOnly summary_revision_contracts authorizes this request to revise such a summary:\nreturn a support observation with summary_revision={supersedes_route_ids,\nprevious_version,reason}, using exact offered route IDs and the current version.\nsummary_revision_contracts.required_source_ids covers replacing ALL offered\neligible_route_ids. When selecting only a subset, retain those selected routes'\nsources, their actual-parent source closure and relevant same-variable counters.\nStructured repair feedback gives the exact required set for that draft's targets.\nThis capability is optional, not a requirement to revise an unchanged summary.\nWith no new observation, return observations=[] unless an outstanding review\nrequires its original draft IDs and sources. For such an unchanged draft, the\nsame sourced support with a valid summary_revision is an idempotent recheck: it\nkeeps the existing routes, ancestry and version, and does not assert new evidence.\nRe-read ALL old and new original premises and relevant counterevidence; retain\nthem in the new support's source_ids and preserve their factual content, negative\nexperiences, conditions and temporal qualifications in the revised whole summary.\nsummary_revision_sources in repair feedback names exact source identities for\nthe selected revision targets, not counts. Re-read and retain EVERY\nrequired_source_ids entry in that feedback; new sources cannot\nreplace missing old identities even if the total citation count is unchanged.\nThe complete missing_source_ids list is structured feedback, not permission to\nfill citations automatically. If the originals actually conflict, return a\nsource-grounded counter or partial/unresolved evidence instead of a revision.\nIn failed_batch_reviews this feedback describes the retained original failed\nobservation; repair_scope describes the current attempted correction.\nretract_ids stays empty. This explicitly retires the older representation, not its\nfacts. Never use revision to hide a genuine contradiction, unavailable evidence,\nor a different scope/parent version. Ordinary facts, terminal choices and audits\ncannot use summary_revision. If a complete compatible account is not supported,\nreturn sourced partial/unresolved instead. Multiple new supports must agree on\none whole value. Existing superseded_by links identify retired representations;\ntheir original evidence remains available. revoked holds actual counterevidence,\nwhich is never erased by a summary revision or ignored through its ancestry.\n\n\nReturn one complete JSON object matching this schema:\n{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"slots\":{\"items\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"oneOf\":[{\"properties\":{\"observations\":{\"items\":{\"allOf\":[{\"if\":{\"properties\":{\"stance\":{\"enum\":[\"support\",\"contradiction\"]}}},\"then\":{\"properties\":{\"entity_scope\":{\"const\":\"user\"},\"time_scope\":{\"const\":\"current\"}}}},{